From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Guido=20G=C3=BCnther?= <agx@sigxcpu.org>
Date: Tue, 20 May 2025 10:35:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/14] broadband-modem-qmi/cellbroadcast: Allow for
 G_MAXUINT16
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

It's a valid channel value. Since start and end are guint16 we can drop
the check altogether.

Fixes: e25dd7db9 ("broadband-modem-qmi: Add support for loading channels")

Signed-off-by: Guido Günther <agx@sigxcpu.org>
(cherry picked from commit 0ccc3fbeec499e217098b22471417b3bab205f72)
---
 src/mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c b/src/mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c
index 0c171cfc..6647de76 100644
--- a/src/mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c
+++ b/src/mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c
@@ -11214,7 +11214,7 @@ cell_broadcast_get_broadcast_config_ready (QmiClientWms *client,
         if (!elem.selected)
             continue;
 
-        if (elem.start >  elem.end || elem.end >= G_MAXUINT16) {
+        if (elem.start > elem.end) {
             g_error_new (MM_CORE_ERROR, MM_CORE_ERROR_FAILED,
                          "Couldn't parse channel interval '%d-%d'", elem.start, elem.end);
             g_task_return_error (task, error);
